[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mServer issues it at login (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mFirst login call has no userId; the API returns one, we persist it, later calls and forms pass it. Authoritative, [39m
     [38;5;246mties to a real account, requires the parameter to be optional on first call.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Existing auth system provides it
     [38;5;246mA session/SSO/backend already hands us an ID before the login form. Cleanest signature — but I don't see such a [39m
     [38;5;246msystem here, so you'd need to point me at it.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m App mints it client-side
     [38;5;246mGenerate a stable ID on first visit, persist it, pass it everywhere including first login. Works with no backend, [39m
     [38;5;246mbut identifies a browser rather than a person.[39m
